## 4. JOURNEY SECTION
White background (`#FFFFFF`), rounded top corners `rounded-t-[40px] sm:rounded-t-[50px] md:rounded-t-[60px]`. Padding: `px-5 sm:px-8 md:px-10 py-20 sm:py-24 md:py-32`.

**Heading**: `"Journey"` in `#0C0C0C`, font-black, uppercase, centered, font size `clamp(3rem, 12vw, 160px)`. Margin bottom: `mb-16 sm:mb-20 md:mb-28`.

**7 items** in a vertical list, `max-w-5xl`, centered. Each item includes an **optional thumbnail image** on the far left (visible on `md:` and up).

### Journey Items:

**01 — Robotics (GART)**
Image: `journey/gart/banner.jpg`
> "Starting as a member, I was immediately drawn into the world of robotics — not because I enjoyed competitions, but because I discovered I could design and build things, turning ideas into reality. From learning mechanical tools and 3D printing my first part to leading a team at Mock GART, each step was new. At FIRST Tech Challenge, I led the mechanics department through the Thanh Hoa Scrimmage to becoming National Champions with a 16-match winning streak and Design Award winners. We continued refining our robot for the World Championship in Texas, reaching Finalist Alliance runner-up in the Edison Division. As Head of Mechanics, I trained a 40-member department, mentored Team Bluebook to win the next Mock GART championship, developed training curricula, taught 34 specialization mentors, and organized GART Camp at the American Embassy's community center."

**02 — EnviroTrack**
Image: `journey/envirotrack/sensor.png`
> "I wanted to use what I learned from competitive robots to tackle Hanoi's most pressing problem: air pollution. I led a team of 3 and built EnviroTrack, a system that measures air quality, displays real-time data publicly, with a mobile app for alerts and predictions. At WICO, experts challenged us to think beyond a complete system and consider real-world deployment. We redesigned it into smaller, independent units and built 25+ refined devices for deployment in markets and train stations across Hanoi and communes in Nam Dinh, hoping people can more easily be aware of the air quality around them."

**03 — Conrad Challenge AUV**
Image: `journey/conrad/auv.jpg`
> "EnviroTrack made me realize I wanted to keep working on environmental problems, but with something more complex. Our team explored microplastic pollution — the lack of accessible, large-scale data on it. We developed an autonomous underwater vehicle capable of diving and mapping microplastic pollution across lakes and coastal areas. I was in charge of electricals and CAD design — accounting for buoyancy, center of gravity, waterproofing, diving, signal transmission, and accurate measurement all at once. After 4 iterations, we built a working prototype and became one of 25 teams selected from 1,000+ to pitch at the Conrad Global Innovation Challenge at Johnson Space Center."

**04 — Samsung SST**
Image: `journey/samsung/code.jpg`
> "I was selected as one of 10 outstanding high school students for Samsung Science and Technology membership at Samsung Vietnam R&D Center. I received mentorship through the Science & Technology Lab, Samsung Innovation Campus coursework, capstone projects, and Korean-language training. I strengthened my foundation in Java and DSA, earned an Advanced level in Samsung's S/W Global Certificate Test, and enrolled in a semiconductor materials fabrication program. For my capstone project, I worked with fellow members to develop a 3D reconstruction tool for preserving artifacts using Gaussian Splatting."

**05 — INS Engineering Internship**
Image: `journey/ins/grid.jpg`
> "During my three-month summer internship at INS Engineering, which provides analytics and studies of power systems for grid operators, I was trained in power grid systems. I learned to read RFIs from customers and calculate, translate, and develop dynamic models of power systems to analyze abnormalities under events such as lightning strikes, power outages, and disconnections. I studied power system physics through online lecture notes, became familiar with macros software for calculations, ETAP for parameter calculation, and PSS/E for model development. More importantly, I learned how professional firms organize teams to work together."

**06 — Research (NDO-MPC)**
Image: `journey/research/gtsd.jpg`
> "As I explored my field, I became interested in control theory for power systems — combining mathematics with simulation and modeling. Under the guidance of Associate Professor Vo Thanh Ha, I researched NDO-MPC control methods for power distribution systems involving batteries and supercapacitors. I built system models, developed the mathematical framework, and evaluated performance through MATLAB simulations. I was especially proud when my research was accepted at the GTSD conference, where I presented to students and received feedback from professors — giving me a clearer understanding of what research actually feels like."

**07 — STEM Outreach (STEMbridge & Volunteering)**
Image: `journey/stembridge/xadan.jpg`
> "I realized how fortunate I was to have access to people, resources, and environment that let me explore STEM beyond school. I founded STEMbridge to create opportunities for students through STEM Fairs, Makerspace donations, and workshops. At Quan Son Boarding School in Lang Son, we built and donated a STEM lab and organized workshops for 300 students. At Xa Dan School for Deaf Students, we adapted activities for different ways of learning and donated educational products. I also volunteered at Cosmosics projects, performing water rocket and holography experiments in Lang Son, and served as a field resetter at the Red River Delta VEX V5 tournaments."

### Item Layout:
Each item: horizontal layout on desktop. Structure (left to right):

1. **Thumbnail** (optional, hidden on mobile `hidden md:block`): `w-[80px] h-[80px] rounded-xl object-cover flex-shrink-0`, hover: `scale-105` transition. Uses the image path from each journey item.
2. **Number**: `font-black`, font size `clamp(3rem, 10vw, 140px)`, color `#0C0C0C`, leading-none, tracking-tighter. Hover: `translate-x-2` transition.
3. **Name + Description** stacked vertically:
   - Name: `font-medium`, uppercase, `tracking-wide`, font size `clamp(1rem, 2.2vw, 2.1rem)`
   - Description: `font-light`, `leading-relaxed`, `max-w-2xl`, font size `clamp(0.85rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem)`, `opacity-60`

Items separated by 1px borders (`rgba(12, 12, 12, 0.15)`) — top border on the container, bottom border on each item. Padding: `py-8 sm:py-10 md:py-12`. Staggered FadeIn: each item delays by `i * 0.1`. Hover: `bg-black/[0.02]` with `transition-colors duration-300`, `px-2 sm:px-4 rounded-xl`.

